# 124. Transition to Unit 5

Unit 4 develops percent as a way to compare a quantity to 100.

For example:

`25% = 25 per 100`

Unit 5 expands this idea into comparisons between many different quantities:

# Ratios, Rates & Proportions

Students will work with:

- ratios;
- equivalent ratios;
- rates;
- unit rates;
- unit prices;
- proportional relationships;
- proportions;
- wages;
- speed;
- recipes;
- scale.

Unit 5 should continue retrieving:

- fractions;
- decimals;
- percent;
- division;
- estimation;
- reasonableness.

The major Unit 5 question becomes:

